+# installed and must stay bare, because it is resolved twice against the
+# single-repo offline mirror (its own header, and deck-nvidia-dry-run.sh fails
+# the build on a qualified name there).
+#
+# Both lists feed this ONLINE download list, and pacman rejects
+# `jupiter-staging/gamescope` together with `gamescope` as a "duplicate target"
+# -- which is exactly how the 4.0.0-stable rebuild first failed (2026-08-15).
+#
+# The QUALIFIED form is the one that must survive here. A bare `gamescope` sent
+# to the online `pacman -Syw` resolves by REPO ORDER, and Valve's repos are
+# appended last on purpose (PROGRESS.md 5.13 measured the alternative: 101
+# overlapping names, Valve older in 50). It would fetch Arch's bare compositor,
+# which ships no usr/share/wayland-sessions/gamescope-wayland.desktop -- the
+# file Gaming Mode's autologin looks for -- and the mistake would be invisible
+# until a target booted into Desktop Mode.
